# Test: the four vrrp show/clear commands resolve and return well-formed
# payloads through the real daemon command path (spec-vrrp-5 AC-8, AC-9; user
# story 3).
#
# This file does NOT boot a LIVE vrrp group behind an external observer, and it
# cannot: an external-plugin observer needs a
# `plugin { external ... }` block, which routes the WHOLE config through the hub
# orchestrator's generic block parser (hub/config.go ParseHubConfig ->
# parseGenericBlock), and that parser rejects the leaf-list `[ ... ]` syntax that
# a vrrp group's mandatory `virtual-address` (and the unit `address`) require
# (verified: "parse config: line N: expected value or '{' after address, got
# LBRACKET"). A config that declares BOTH an external observer AND a live group
# is unparseable by the daemon, and the SSH `ze cli` alternative needs the ze_ssh
# build tag that the needs-linux QEMU binary is not built with. The live
# elected-master path (macvlan +
# virtual MAC + VIP install + FSM->Master + teardown) is proven by KERNEL
# readback in test/vrrp/vrrp-instance-up.ci, the populated show/statistics
# payload SHAPES by internal/plugins/vrrp/cmd_show_test.go, and THIS file now
# owns the remaining functional gap those two cannot reach: that all four
# commands are reachable end-to-end through the live daemon dispatch path.
#
# VALIDATES: with the vrrp plugin loaded on the shared `interface` root, an
# external observer dispatches each command through the real path (CLI YANG
# dispatch -> RPC proxy ForwardToPlugin -> engine OnExecuteCommand ->
# handleCommand, cmd_show.go) and gets the documented envelope back:
#   AC-8 -- `show vrrp` -> {"vrrp": [...]}, `show vrrp interface name <if>` ->
#   the same shape filtered to one parent, `show vrrp statistics` ->
#   {"vrrp-statistics": [...]}. Every wire method (ze-show:vrrp,
#   ze-show:vrrp-interface, ze-show:vrrp-statistics) is registered on the daemon
#   and the proxy FORWARDS rather than re-dispatching (no recursion).
#   AC-9 -- `clear vrrp statistics` -> {"cleared": N} reports how many instances
#   it cleared.
# With zero groups configured the engine is idle, so every list payload is EMPTY
# and `cleared` is 0 -- which also exercises AC-6's "show vrrp reports zero
# instances" clause through the real dispatch path (not just the config surface
# that test/vrrp/vrrp-idle.ci covers on darwin).
# PREVENTS: a show/clear wire method that fails to resolve on the daemon command
# path (the exact regression the .ci layer catches that a handler unit test
# cannot -- unit tests call handleCommand directly and never exercise the YANG
# node -> proxy -> ForwardToPlugin hop), a proxy that re-dispatches into
# recursion, or a payload whose top-level key drifts from the CLI contract.
#
# option=needs-linux: the daemon runs the interface plugin's netlink backend,
# which needs Linux (on darwin it fails config apply and the daemon never boots).
#
# The observer is spawned as a BGP peer `process` (with a ze-peer connection),
# the established external-observer pattern (test/plugin/ddos-show.ci,
# anomaly-show.ci, bfd-json-show.ci): a top-level `plugin { external }` alone
# fails with "no TLS acceptor configured (hub config required for external
# plugins)"; attaching it under a peer process gives it the engine connection it
# needs. The bgp/interface config here carries no leaf-lists, so the hub
# orchestrator's generic block parser accepts it.
option=needs-linux

# ze-peer: accept ze's outbound connection so the peer (and its observer process)
# establishes.
stdin=peer:terminator=EOF_PEER
option=tcp_connections:value=1
option=timeout:value=15s
option=asn:value=65001
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF00170200000000
EOF_PEER


stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	external vrrp-show {
		run "ze-test fixture vrrp/vrrp-show"
		encoder json
	}
}

interface {
	backend netlink;
}

bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				accept false
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 65000
				remote 65001
			}
			router-id 1.2.3.4
			family {
				ipv4/unicast {
					prefix {
						maximum 10000
					}
				}
			}
			capability {
				graceful-restart disable
			}
		}
		behavior {
			group-updates disable
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

option=env:var=ze.log.vrrp:value=info

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze-peer --port $PORT:stdin=peer
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=30s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=OK: vrrp show/interface/statistics/clear all resolve through the daemon path
